<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa Cargo Feb load factor down 1.8pc.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa Cargo Feb load factor down 1.8pc.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa Cargo AG recorded a 1.8 percentage point drop in its freight load factor to 68.3 percent in February, parent company Deutsche Lufthansa AG said.</p>
<p>The cumulative cargo load factor over the first two months of 1997 was 66.1 percent, a fall of 1.2 percentage points, the latest Lufthansa investor relations monthly traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following table shows Lufthansa Cargo traffic for February 1997.</p>
<p> Cargo/mail (1,000 tonnes)	  126.4  down 1.8 pct</p>
<p> Available cargo tonne-km(million)    702    up   2.4</p>
<p> Revenue cargo tonne-km(million)	480    down 0.3</p>
<p> Cargo load factor		     68.3  down 1.8 pts</p>
<p> Europe(1,000 t)			 57.8  down 4.7</p>
<p> Americas(1,000 t)		     34.7  up   3.0</p>
<p> Asia-Pacific(1,000 t)		 29.5  down 2.7</p>
<p>The following table shows Lufthansa Cargo cumulative traffic for January-February 1997.</p>
<p> Cargo/mail(1,000 tonnes)	   246.9  down 1.6 pct</p>
<p> Available cargo tonne-km(million)  1,412    up   2.5</p>
<p> Revenue cargo tonne-km(million)	933    up   0.7</p>
<p> Cargo load factor		     66.1  down 1.2 pts</p>
<p> Europe(1,000 t)			114.2  down 3.8</p>
<p> Americas(1,000 t)		     65.7  up   1.7</p>
<p> Asia-Pacific(1,000 t)		 59.9  up   1.4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
